 "salt": "8lJtqWczo-XaPvA3QhsL-w==",
 "text": "Prophecy is a religious ritual. The difference between a prophecy and an omen is where it comes from. A prophecy is the result of a ritual begun to find information about the future. An omen is an unsought gift. The flight of birds was an omen, and interpreting it was a skill of the druids. Prophecy could be courted by initiates. The druids used ritual techniques that produced a trance. This state permitted a view into hidden matters. Prophecy is a specialized form of divination. In Ireland rituals included the imbas forosnai and the bull-sleep, in which a druid dreamed the future inside a bull's hide.",
